>     \[
>     err_6 = \frac{\gamma}{\left( \frac{allvals9[\text{AvoidedImpact}][ii]}{\left( \frac{allvals9[\text{TotalBenefits} / \text{AdaptationCost}][ii] \times allvals9[\text{AdaptationCost}][ii]}{allvals9[\text{AdaptationCost}][ii]} \right)} \right)} - 1
>     \]
> 
> ### Overall Error Metric
> 
> The overall function to be minimized remains:
> 
> \[
> \text{minimize} \quad \sqrt{\sum_{k=0}^{n} err_k^2} = \sqrt{err_0^2 + err_1^2 + err_2^2 + err_3^2 + err_3b^2 + err_3c^2 + err_3d^2 + err_4^2 + err_4b^2 + err_5^2 + err_5b^2 + err_6^2}
> \]
> 
> This setup allows for the systematic minimization of the combined error across all relevant economic relationships, ensuring a robust estimation of the adaptation metrics.
